<Base title="About Stardew Tips" description="An independent Stardew Valley field guide, maintained by Holly, with practical reading paths for new and returning farmers."><div class="simple-page container"><p class="eyebrow">HELLO, FARMER</p><h1>A small guide to a big little world.</h1><p>Stardew Tips is an independent English-language guide site maintained by Holly. We focus on the decisions that can make a new farm feel overwhelming: where to spend your first gold, which seasonal items to keep, and how to leave enough energy for exploring.</p><h2>What you will find here</h2><p>Our library covers getting started, farming, fishing, mining, and community life. Start with the <a href="/start-here/">new farmer’s reading path</a> choose a <a href="/plans/">goal-based reading plan</a>, or browse <a href="/guides/">all guides by topic and farm stage</a>. Each article has a publication date and a contents list so you can get to the relevant section.</p><h2>Practical, with room for your own choices</h2><p>We explain tradeoffs rather than promise a perfect save. A profitable crop may be a poor fit for your watering time. A fast mining route may require equipment you do not yet own. Our guides aim to make those assumptions visible.</p><h2>Accountability</h2><p>Read our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> for scope, references, writing tools, and corrections. Questions and error reports go directly to <a href="mailto:holly125@yeah.net">holly125@yeah.net</a>.</p><h2>Funding and affiliation</h2><p>The site is free to read and is intended to be funded through display advertising, subject to Google AdSense approval. Stardew Tips is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by ConcernedApe. Stardew Valley and game artwork belong to their respective rights holders.</p></div></Base>
